  "body": "## What changed\n\n`cargo xtask release --version X.Y.Z --no-tag [--title T] [--skip-gate] [--skip-build] [--installer] [--dry-run]` ports `scripts/release.ps1`'s ten phases into xtask (`xtask/src/release.rs`, `release_bump.rs`, `release_pack.rs`, tests in `release_tests.rs`). `scripts/release.ps1` is now a thin wrapper forwarding its old switches. AGENTS.md (release step 2, the fix-only hand-test line) and `scripts/README.md` name `cargo xtask release`; `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 7 -> 8. No new dependency (regex was already xtask's).\n\nPer OS:\n- **Windows**: as before - `sign.ps1` (phase 7), zip staged in Rust + `Compress-Archive` (phase 8), `installer.ps1` on `--installer` (phase 9).\n- **Linux / macOS / FreeBSD**: phase 8 runs `scripts/package-linux.sh` / `package-macos.sh` / `package-freebsd.sh` (macOS builds both architectures in phase 5, as release.yml does); phase 7 is skipped by name; `--installer` is refused by name before phase 1. Any other OS is refused by name.\n\n**Windows exe lock (#750 review):** the cut never builds the xtask package while it runs. The gate runs in process (`plan::release` through `exec::Run`, not a nested `cargo xtask gate release`, which would `cargo run -p xtask` and relink the running exe), and the release build names `-p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post` instead of the whole workspace (pinned by `release_build_never_builds_xtask`).\n\n## Deliberate differences from release.ps1 (also in docs/decisions/749-xtask-release.md)\n- Gate phase runs the current `gate release` tier (13 steps, incl. the ui snapshot lane) instead of the old script's own 6-command list.\n- Build phase builds the product packages only (release.yml's list), not `cargo build --release` of the workspace.\n- Cargo.lock: workspace path packages bumped in Rust, then still `cargo update -w -q` and the version-lines-only diff guard.\n- Zip carries `NOTICE`, as release.yml's does (the old local script left it out); asset dirs copied recursively.\n- No tag code path: the old script already refused every tagging run (\"main is branch-protected\"); same message kept. Commit messages and trailer kept verbatim.\n- AGENTS.md's hand-test line said `release.ps1 -NoTag` \"on main\", which the script refuses; it now says a scratch branch off main.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 23 passed (13 existing + 10 new). Pinning tests: `bump_toml_moves_only_the_workspace_version`, `bump_lock_moves_workspace_packages_not_registry_ones`, `lock_diff_guard_takes_version_lines_only`, `notes_need_this_versions_section_above_the_history`, `preflight_ignores_the_files_the_cut_commits`, `zip_layout_mirrors_release_yml` (staged file list + a real stage copy), `release_build_never_builds_xtask`, `parse_takes_release_ps1s_switches`, `dry_run_walks_the_ten_phases_and_changes_nothing` (fixture git repo, Windows and Linux phase lists), `refusals_are_named`.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Dry-run parity on Windows (RELEASE_NOTES.md temporarily topped with a 9.9.9 section, both exit 0): `cargo xtask release --version 9.9.9 --no-tag --dry-run` vs origin/main's `release.ps1 -Version 9.9.9 -NoTag -DryRun`. Same ten phase banners, same preflight, bump, commit, verify, sign, installer and summary lines; diffs only in the deliberate items above (gate step list, `-p` build, NOTICE + file count in the stage line, `Compress-Archive` shown with its powershell invocation, `--flag` spelling). Same again through the new wrapper with `-Installer -SkipGate` (installer lines identical). Wrapper without `-NoTag` refuses with the old message.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No real cut: no bump, commit, release build, signing, zip or installer was run (only dry runs and the fixture stage copy).\n- Linux, macOS and FreeBSD paths ran only as unit-test dry runs on Windows (`Os::Linux` plan); the package-*.sh hand-off was not executed on those hosts.\n- Release gate tier not run (per brief).\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #749\nFixes #748\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
